International hypocrisy deepens over Palestinian suffering in Gaza: Analyst
Journalist and author Sakina Datoo describes Gaza’s humanitarian catastrophe as an unprecedented tragedy, condemning the international community’s continued inaction as displaced Palestinians face yet another winter without adequate shelter.
@PressTV

US took ‘a giant step back in history,’ Trump says after midterm defeat
US President Donald Trump has described the Republicans’ defeat in the midterm elections as “a giant step back in history,” as he suggested he could dismiss some officials and make a few changes in his cabinet.
@PressTV

Scabies affects 80% of Palestinian prisoners in Israeli jails, advocacy group says
The Palestinian Prisoner Society says widespread scabies infections, overcrowding, inadequate medical care and repeated violent raids are worsening conditions for Palestinian detainees, including children and women, in Israeli prisons.
@PressTV

Yemen’s Armed Forces: Saudi aggression launches 91 airstrikes and missiles in 24 hours
Yemen’s Armed Forces said Saudi-led coalition forces carried out 91 air strikes and missile attacks over the past 24 hours across six governorates, targeting civilian sites and causing casualties among Yemeni civilians.
@PressTV

‘Hegseth has got to Go’: US lawmakers demand ouster of Pentagon chief over ‘reckless war of choice’ against Iran
House Minority Leader Hakeem Jeffries has declared that US War Secretary Pete Hegseth “has got to go,” saying the Pentagon chief abused power and engineered a costly war of aggression against the Islamic Republic of Iran that has inflicted economic pain on the American people and failed to advance any legitimate security interest.
@PressTV

Afghan returnees face uncertain future after deportation from Pakistan
Abdullah Amirzada reports from Kabul
@PressTV

Hamas says Israeli blockade worsens Gaza’s winter humanitarian crisis
Hamas says Israel’s continued blockade and obstruction of the ceasefire’s humanitarian protocol have exacerbated the suffering of hundreds of thousands of displaced Palestinians in the besieged Gaza Strip amid severe winter weather, flooding, and damage to shelters.
@PressTV

Yemen strikes targets deep inside Saudi Arabia to deter aggression
Yemeni armed forces have carried out four major operations deep inside Saudi Arabia and in Yemeni provinces where Saudi troops are present to deter ‘Saudi aggression’ and inflict ‘significant pain’ on the kingdom.
@PressTV
